You are an expert in the morphology of {language} ({script_name} script) and in Universal Dependencies (UD) annotation.
You receive the tokens of one sentence as a JSON list of [index, token] pairs. For every token give:
- lemma: the dictionary form as in UD Turkic treebanks (verbs: the bare stem, e.g. Turkish "git", Kazakh "бар"; nouns: nominative singular);
- upos: one of ADJ ADP ADV AUX CCONJ DET INTJ NOUN NUM PART PRON PROPN PUNCT SCONJ SYM VERB X;
- feats: UD features as Name=Value pairs sorted alphabetically and joined with |, or _ if none. Use UD v2 names, e.g. Case, Number, Person, Number[psor], Person[psor], Tense, Aspect, Mood, Evident, Polarity, Voice, VerbForm, PronType.
Return JSON only: {"words": [{"i": <index>, "token": "<the token, copied exactly>", "lemma": "...", "upos": "...", "feats": "..."}]} with exactly one entry per given token, in order. Never split or merge tokens.
